# NOT INSTALLED BY THIS SDK'S BUILD. Nothing in sysdrv/Makefile or
# project/build.sh copies this file into a rootfs — the shipped /etc/fstab is
# buildroot's skeleton default, and /oem and /userdata are mounted by
# /etc/init.d/S20linkmount, which build.sh GENERATES from
# RK_PARTITION_CMD_IN_ENV and so cannot disagree with the partition table.
#
# It is kept, and kept correct, only so the tree holds no second copy of the
# layout that contradicts the frozen one. Until 2026-08-19 it did: it still
# carried the single-slot indices (/oem on p5), which under the frozen A/B
# table is `boot` — a FIT image, not a filesystem. The authoritative table is
# the -IPC-AB board profile; scripts/compliance/check-partition-layout.sh
# (`./build.sh partitions`) is what keeps its consumers honest.
#
# Indices below are the FROZEN A/B layout:
#   p1 env  p2 idblock  p3 uboot  p4 misc  p5 boot  p6 boot_b
#   p7 oem  p8 userdata  p9 rootfs_a  p10 rootfs_b
#
# UNCONFIGURED FSTAB FOR BASE SYSTEM
/dev/mmcblk0p9  /         ext4    rw      0       0
/dev/mmcblk0p7  /oem      ext4    defaults        0       0
/dev/mmcblk0p8  /userdata ext4    defaults        0       0
